From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jens Willmer <info@jwillmer.de>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 12:23:56 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 081/111] Open <details> keyed by their source, not their
 position

A <details> with the same summary added above another in the same section
still moved the open state to the wrong block. The key now also holds a
hash of the block's source; the occurrence count only tells apart blocks
that are identical. Editing an open block's source closes it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

diff --git a/src/markdown_html.rs b/src/markdown_html.rs
index 3aa21b0..28dfedc 100644
--- a/src/markdown_html.rs
+++ b/src/markdown_html.rs
@@ -142,14 +142,16 @@ pub struct Picture {
 }
 
 /// Which `<details>` it is, so its open state stays with it when blocks are added or removed
-/// above: the heading it sits under, the text of its summary and, as summaries can repeat, how
-/// many with the same summary come before it under that heading. A `<details>` added in another
-/// section does not move the open state; only one added above it in its own section does.
+/// above: the heading it sits under, the text of its summary, a hash of its source and, only for
+/// blocks that are the same in all of these, how many come before it. A `<details>` added above
+/// does not move the open state unless it is a copy; editing the block closes it.
 #[derive(Clone, Debug, PartialEq, Eq, Hash)]
 pub struct DetailsKey {
     /// Text of the nearest Markdown heading above, empty above the first.
     pub heading: String,
     pub summary: String,
+    /// Hash of the block's source, from `<details>` to `</details>`.
+    pub body: u64,
     pub occurrence: usize,
 }
 
